+## Check frozen effort settings
+
+Before a run, check the effective effort settings against the values frozen for that
+case. Supply `--check` with one or more repeatable `--expect lane=value` options:
+
+```sh
+python3 plugins/astral-orchestrator/scripts/configure-effort.py \
+  --settings-file /path/to/effort-levels.toml \
+  --check \
+  --expect orchestrator=high \
+  --expect luna=xhigh \
+  --expect terra=xhigh \
+  --expect reviewer=high
+```
+
+The lanes are `orchestrator`, `luna`, `terra`, and `reviewer`; the allowed values are
+`minimal`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max`, and `ultra`. Check mode requires at
+least one expectation and cannot be combined with settings changes. It always emits a
+compact JSON report with `changed: false`, the current `effort` values, requested
+`expected` values, the settings-file path and presence, `matched`, and any
+`mismatches`. It exits zero only when every expectation matches; a mismatch or invalid
+expectation exits non-zero. Check mode only reads the supplied settings file: it never
+creates, writes, or changes it.
+
 The control is `single-sol`: one Sol route. The treatment is `astral`: an orchestrator,
 at least one Luna or Terra worker, and a fresh Sol reviewer. Record observed route facts
 for every lane rather than assuming that a task label proves its model or effort.
